WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
Antimatter sounds like science fiction.

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.290
Yet hospitals put it to work.

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.740
PET scans rely on positrons,
which come out of beta-plus decay.

4
00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.910
A positron is the
antiparticle of the electron:

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.960
its antimatter twin.

6
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.530
So what is actually different
about an antiparticle?

7
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.340
How could you tell it
from its ordinary twin?

8
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.890
In this mission, you'll meet
antimatter's best-known particle,

9
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.710
the positron, and where it comes from.

10
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.770
Then you'll fire a beam of electrons
between two charged plates,

11
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.460
and predict the path of a positron beam.

12
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: find out how to tell
an antiparticle from its twin.
